WEBVTT

00:12.180 --> 00:14.050
Hang on tight to that bundle!

00:14.050 --> 00:15.290
Of course!

00:16.030 --> 00:17.500
Sir Witch!

00:17.500 --> 00:19.360
The bridge is right by that tree!

00:25.420 --> 00:27.470
Please take me, too!

00:27.470 --> 00:29.160
I'll be useful.

00:29.160 --> 00:30.220
I promise!

00:32.160 --> 00:33.290
Agott.

00:34.220 --> 00:36.890
This won't be like your lessons.

00:37.400 --> 00:39.980
There will be a lot of people there 
who aren't witches, too.

00:40.380 --> 00:46.010
You haven't even taken the second test 
to be allowed to cast in front of them.

00:46.010 --> 00:47.390
So for now—

00:48.360 --> 00:50.610
If you don't let me go now, then when?!

00:50.610 --> 00:52.870
I've been practicing 
on my own, constantly!

00:52.870 --> 00:55.370
I know how to cast in front of people!

00:55.370 --> 00:58.750
I've been preparing for the test for ages!

00:58.750 --> 01:03.750
Shouldn't a master seek more opportunities 
for his apprentices to gain experience?!

01:04.210 --> 01:05.940
Even so...

01:05.940 --> 01:07.510
Please, hurry!

01:08.070 --> 01:10.140
We have to get back as soon as we can!

01:11.020 --> 01:12.510
I'll go on ahead.

01:12.850 --> 01:16.010
I'll set up a Windowway exit at the site.

01:17.660 --> 01:20.140
Ready the medicine and contraptions 
we'll need, and meet me there.

01:20.850 --> 01:22.620
I'll take Agott ahead with me.

01:23.940 --> 01:25.920
I'll get my cloak and hat!

01:29.370 --> 01:30.710
We're coming, too!

01:34.080 --> 01:36.200
Relax already.

01:36.830 --> 01:39.610
There are things you can learn 
from experiencing reality, too.

01:40.530 --> 01:42.080
I'm worried.

01:42.880 --> 01:44.580
Agott, in particular...

01:44.940 --> 01:47.090
She focuses not on the joy 
of what she's accomplished,

01:47.090 --> 01:49.840
but the frustration of things 
she can't yet do.

01:53.050 --> 01:55.220
<i>There's nothing wrong 
with being inexperienced.</i>

01:56.450 --> 01:58.240
<i>But in her haste to grow up...</i>

02:00.130 --> 02:03.060
<i>I fear she may take a wrong step.</i>

02:09.430 --> 02:11.400
The ground here isn't stable.

02:11.770 --> 02:13.710
There it is! Over there!

04:00.640 --> 04:05.810
<b>Who Is Magic For?</b>

04:04.630 --> 04:05.890
Are those...

04:07.840 --> 04:09.650
Witches!

04:10.270 --> 04:12.750
Thank goodness. We're saved!

04:12.750 --> 04:15.240
Hey! The witches are here!

04:15.240 --> 04:16.390
Agott.

04:17.540 --> 04:19.480
You know how to use these, right?

04:20.700 --> 04:23.280
Help the people dry their clothes.

04:23.670 --> 04:25.420
Once that's done, await further orders.

04:27.160 --> 04:30.770
You just want me to use 
magic contraptions?

04:30.770 --> 04:31.900
Isn't there something more—

04:31.900 --> 04:33.290
That's all.

04:33.960 --> 04:36.320
What else did you expect?

04:37.430 --> 04:39.830
You think simple tasks 
aren't worth doing?

04:40.940 --> 04:43.180
I can see why Qifrey was worried.

04:44.560 --> 04:45.810
Agott...

04:47.620 --> 04:49.310
You're too impatient.

04:51.270 --> 04:53.340
If you want to show off what you can do,

04:53.340 --> 04:55.190
there will be other, better settings.

04:55.830 --> 04:59.570
But if you want to be useful here and now,

04:59.840 --> 05:03.450
think carefully about what magic is for.

05:08.330 --> 05:12.590
<i>He's treating me like 
an ignorant child again.</i>

05:09.230 --> 05:10.020
Hey.

05:10.020 --> 05:11.440
Thanks, Olly.

05:13.660 --> 05:15.720
<i>I work harder than anyone,</i>

05:15.720 --> 05:18.340
<i>but it means nothing if I don't 
have something to show for it!</i>

05:19.000 --> 05:22.590
<i>I need to prove to that person 
as soon as possible...</i>

05:23.180 --> 05:26.530
<i>that I'm a worthy witch.</i>

05:31.710 --> 05:32.850
Qifrey!

05:48.380 --> 05:49.910
Amazing!

05:49.910 --> 05:51.760
That's incredible!

05:51.760 --> 05:53.760
He parted the river with a sword!

05:53.760 --> 05:57.040
It's not safe! Please, stand back!

05:57.410 --> 05:59.630
Olruggio! How many in the carriage?!

05:59.630 --> 06:02.760
Two! I'm carrying the first out now!

06:07.810 --> 06:09.640
This isn't easy.

06:10.280 --> 06:12.310
This is why I hate water!

06:12.730 --> 06:14.060
Hold the line!

06:14.060 --> 06:15.850
I'm moving as fast as I can!

06:18.170 --> 06:19.020
There.

06:19.020 --> 06:20.090
Ready!

06:20.090 --> 06:21.530
Got it!

06:41.650 --> 06:42.840
Well done.

06:43.690 --> 06:45.220
They're all safe.

06:45.220 --> 06:46.430
Great work.

06:50.640 --> 06:51.680
Custas!

06:51.940 --> 06:53.180
Dagda!

06:56.650 --> 06:57.880
I'm sorry.

06:57.880 --> 07:01.010
I was trying to protect your cargo...

07:01.690 --> 07:04.440
It doesn't matter, 
as long as you're safe.

07:06.760 --> 07:09.690
I really can't thank you enough!

07:09.690 --> 07:12.370
No problem. I'm glad we made it in time.

07:13.080 --> 07:17.520
My apprentices brought medicine, 
so if you're injured, go...

07:19.390 --> 07:22.210
Awesome!

07:22.210 --> 07:24.030
That's so cool!

07:22.210 --> 07:23.480
Incredible.

07:24.030 --> 07:25.430
I was just curious to see it.

07:25.430 --> 07:27.630
This is the coolest thing ever!

07:27.630 --> 07:30.220
Master Qifrey, what <i>is</i> this?!

07:32.060 --> 07:35.050
This is the Raincleaver.

07:37.270 --> 07:40.860
The pattern inscribed on the blade 
is made up of Casting Seals.

07:41.480 --> 07:44.090
As small as they are, 
with this many seals,

07:44.090 --> 07:46.740
you could even carve a 
path through the ocean.

07:48.110 --> 07:50.190
Master Qifrey!

07:50.190 --> 07:52.150
Can I hold it for a second?!

07:52.150 --> 07:53.290
You may not.

07:53.950 --> 07:57.790
Magic cast on weapons 
requires the utmost caution.

07:58.750 --> 08:03.120
It's not safe, so I can't 
let you handle it just yet.

08:05.020 --> 08:06.300
Qifrey!

08:06.630 --> 08:09.800
I'm going to check upriver 
just to be sure.

08:10.190 --> 08:13.350
I'll check on the downriver damage, then.

08:13.690 --> 08:15.630
Tetia, come with me.

08:16.240 --> 08:17.490
Yes, Master!

08:17.490 --> 08:18.790
Richeh, you're with me.

08:18.790 --> 08:19.600
Right.

08:21.220 --> 08:23.600
You two, watch over things here.

08:23.600 --> 08:24.820
We'll be back in no time!

08:24.820 --> 08:26.640
Sure thing!

08:37.980 --> 08:39.970
<i>This is totally awkward.</i>

08:40.830 --> 08:44.220
<i>I need to fix and return Agott's 
Sylph Shoes as soon as I can.</i>

08:46.290 --> 08:48.300
There, all done.

08:48.300 --> 08:51.340
Thanks a lot, Little Miss Witch.

08:53.830 --> 08:56.600
<i>Little Miss Witch?</i>

08:56.600 --> 08:59.730
Little Miss Witch!

09:00.080 --> 09:01.620
There we go.

09:02.190 --> 09:07.590
Still... half of the cargo got swept away.

09:07.590 --> 09:10.330
Custas! What are you doing?!

09:10.330 --> 09:11.490
Get back here!

09:11.490 --> 09:12.990
Custas!

09:12.990 --> 09:15.000
Don't worry, Dagda!

09:15.000 --> 09:17.240
There's a gap in the bank here.

09:17.240 --> 09:20.000
One of our crates got caught on it.

09:20.000 --> 09:22.550
I'll pick it up and be right back!

09:25.000 --> 09:26.170
You idiot!

09:26.170 --> 09:29.380
There's a gap because the bank collapsed!

09:29.910 --> 09:31.380
Get back here this instant!

09:31.380 --> 09:32.840
Custas!

09:52.910 --> 09:55.370
N-No...

09:55.850 --> 09:57.810
Custas... no...

09:57.810 --> 09:59.560
No, Mister Dagda!

09:59.560 --> 10:01.320
It'll just collapse further!

10:01.320 --> 10:02.580
Let me go!

10:02.580 --> 10:04.760
Custas! Custas!

10:03.420 --> 10:04.760
Agott!

10:09.060 --> 10:10.150
Coco?

10:11.440 --> 10:13.050
She wasn't... buri—

10:13.050 --> 10:14.640
Agott!

10:14.640 --> 10:15.800
I'm here!

10:15.800 --> 10:17.070
Over here!

10:18.710 --> 10:19.590
Hey!

10:19.590 --> 10:21.890
Are you all right? Were you hurt?

10:21.890 --> 10:24.160
I'm... fine.

10:25.540 --> 10:26.620
But...

10:26.620 --> 10:27.900
Custas!

10:28.310 --> 10:30.760
Answer me! Custas!

10:33.070 --> 10:35.010
Custas!

10:36.420 --> 10:37.550
No...

10:39.500 --> 10:41.380
What do I... Wha...

10:42.630 --> 10:44.210
Of course.

10:45.370 --> 10:48.090
There's a witch right here!

10:49.290 --> 10:53.030
Please! You can use magic 
to save him, right?!

10:53.830 --> 10:57.220
I'm begging you! Please save him!

11:00.260 --> 11:02.970
<i>This is... my chance.</i>

11:03.870 --> 11:05.850
<i>Our masters aren't here.</i>

11:05.850 --> 11:08.410
<i>I can't call them back here 
without my Sylph Shoes.</i>

11:08.410 --> 11:11.860
<i>Coco's locked down, 
and the situation is desperate.</i>

11:12.320 --> 11:17.720
<i>If I save him with magic, I can prove 
that they were wrong about me...</i>

11:17.720 --> 11:18.990
Miss.

11:19.840 --> 11:22.650
Will you be casting a spell this time?

11:23.370 --> 11:25.970
She said she'd use magic to save him!

11:25.970 --> 11:27.980
What kind of spell will she use?

11:27.980 --> 11:31.300
Stop it! Custas is in danger down there!

11:33.160 --> 11:35.730
Now, show what you can do, Agott.

11:38.650 --> 11:41.890
Is this all the magic she has?

11:44.680 --> 11:47.340
Not much, compared to the others.

11:47.340 --> 11:49.330
You need to take the 
drawing more seriously.

11:49.330 --> 11:52.120
She's not bad, but... she's average.

11:52.120 --> 11:54.230
I would hardly believe 
she's <i>her</i> daughter.

11:54.230 --> 11:56.380
When someone has talent, 
you can tell by this age.

11:56.380 --> 11:57.940
Is she even practicing?

11:57.940 --> 11:59.790
She's still just a child.

12:00.930 --> 12:03.190
I had such high hopes.

12:03.190 --> 12:05.400
But you've disappointed me, Agott.

12:05.400 --> 12:07.030
I won't take you as an apprentice.

12:07.030 --> 12:10.440
Our family has no need
for someone with no talent.

12:16.860 --> 12:19.090
<i>Why do I have to remember that now?</i>

12:19.090 --> 12:21.540
<i>At a time like this... Why?!</i>

12:23.890 --> 12:25.350
Agott!

12:26.420 --> 12:28.480
Hey, is there anything...

12:29.210 --> 12:32.110
Anything I can do from here?!

12:36.410 --> 12:38.740
I want to save Custas!

12:38.740 --> 12:41.740
Is there anything I can do?!

12:44.240 --> 12:46.240
But if you want to be useful here and now,

12:47.010 --> 12:50.830
think carefully about what magic is for.

12:53.630 --> 12:55.380
Coco! Can you move?!

12:55.680 --> 12:57.570
Give me the whole situation!

12:57.980 --> 13:00.760
Um... well...

13:00.760 --> 13:04.820
I'm in a gap in the bank, 
and the current's a lot slower here.

13:04.820 --> 13:07.340
I don't think it'll sweep me away.

13:07.340 --> 13:13.300
But it's so muddy, I keep slipping, 
and I can't climb back up.

13:13.900 --> 13:16.300
Custas is unconscious,

13:16.300 --> 13:19.280
and he's pinned by a rock I don't think 
even a grown-up could move.

13:21.680 --> 13:23.000
And...

13:26.330 --> 13:31.470
<i>I can't let non-witches 
see me drawing spells.</i>

13:32.140 --> 13:33.420
<i>What do I do?</i>

13:33.420 --> 13:34.960
Agott!

13:35.980 --> 13:37.570
<i>What do I do here?!</i>

13:46.510 --> 13:48.060
Easthies.

13:48.060 --> 13:50.860
There's been a report from a village 
on the outskirts of Kalhn.

13:50.860 --> 13:55.680
A huge pillar of water was seen 
in the Marshwoods upriver.

13:57.560 --> 13:58.730
Let's go.

14:03.530 --> 14:07.780
<i>The situation is utterly dire, 
but she hasn't given up.</i>

14:11.700 --> 14:14.040
<i>If I could just use magic...</i>

14:15.840 --> 14:16.790
Agott!

14:17.700 --> 14:20.550
Hey, do you have that? That thing!

14:20.550 --> 14:21.670
Thing?

14:21.670 --> 14:25.790
That thing! You know, Master Olruggio's...

14:26.530 --> 14:27.390
The rings!

14:28.050 --> 14:30.930
Of course! The Link Rings!

14:33.400 --> 14:34.770
<i>With these...</i>

14:36.250 --> 14:40.390
<i>If I can just dry my paper, I can use my 
newly learned spell to levitate the rock</i>

14:40.390 --> 14:42.680
<i>and save Custas!</i>

14:43.810 --> 14:47.280
<i>But Coco can't do it.</i>

14:48.360 --> 14:52.040
<i>When you need to draw a 
spell in front of Outsiders,</i>

14:52.040 --> 14:56.020
<i>you have to hide your hands 
beneath your long cloak...</i>

14:56.800 --> 15:00.630
<i>and draw only with the muscle 
memory of your fingers.</i>

15:08.050 --> 15:09.860
What's she doing?

15:08.940 --> 15:11.020
Maybe it takes her more time 
because she's young...

15:09.860 --> 15:11.990
I'm glad there are still 
witches here, but...

15:11.020 --> 15:11.990
Listen, everyone!

15:15.990 --> 15:18.310
I am Qifrey's top apprentice,

15:18.610 --> 15:21.320
the witch Agott Arklaum.

15:21.740 --> 15:26.320
Behold my incredible magical gifts!

15:28.780 --> 15:34.710
<i>All of that practice—so that I wouldn't 
be afraid when it was time to act.</i>

15:37.330 --> 15:39.190
<i>Even if Coco can't do it...</i>

15:40.590 --> 15:41.990
<i>I can!</i>

15:59.820 --> 16:01.190
Wow...

16:09.620 --> 16:12.700
<i>I was just practicing the levitation 
spell with the carapace yam.</i>

16:15.040 --> 16:17.330
Even I can handle this!

16:23.090 --> 16:24.420
It won't work.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.810
<i>Having just practiced 
it so much, I know...</i>

16:28.160 --> 16:31.090
<i>To move a stone this large and heavy,</i>

16:31.800 --> 16:33.910
<i>the Palm Quire's paper is too small.</i>

16:36.680 --> 16:38.350
Custas!

16:38.350 --> 16:41.000
H-Huh? What was I...

16:41.400 --> 16:43.860
You're awake! I'm so glad!

16:43.860 --> 16:45.690
Who are you?

16:45.690 --> 16:48.170
I'm Coco. I'm a witch.

16:48.170 --> 16:50.310
We both fell from the cliff.

16:50.700 --> 16:51.870
Do you remember?

16:53.700 --> 16:57.250
So... I'm still alive?

16:57.960 --> 17:02.670
I saw a bird made of light, 
so I felt sure I was dead...

17:02.670 --> 17:04.040
Oh, that?

17:04.040 --> 17:07.630
That was magic! My friend's spell!

17:09.170 --> 17:11.270
My friend's spell...

17:11.270 --> 17:12.840
That's it!

17:15.350 --> 17:18.480
<i>This won't distract them for long.</i>

17:18.480 --> 17:19.410
<i>Hurry!</i>

17:19.410 --> 17:20.540
Excuse me.

17:20.850 --> 17:24.690
That spell is very beautiful, 
but is that all it can do?

17:24.690 --> 17:28.860
All you did was make a light show! 
You didn't accomplish anything!

17:29.340 --> 17:33.870
Can't it carry a person down there, 
or fly down there and bring him up?!

17:34.120 --> 17:35.470
Well...

17:36.050 --> 17:38.870
Enough! I'll climb down there 
and save him myself!

17:39.570 --> 17:41.240
<i>If he looks down there now...</i>

17:42.050 --> 17:44.540
No! You can't go!

17:54.990 --> 17:57.710
P-Pull me in!

17:57.710 --> 18:00.210
I-I can't get down!

18:00.580 --> 18:02.810
R-Right...

18:03.810 --> 18:05.180
Custas!

18:05.990 --> 18:08.150
Custas! Custas!

18:10.680 --> 18:11.370
Is he all right?

18:11.370 --> 18:12.320
Was he hurt?

18:19.380 --> 18:20.610
It's floating! It's floating!

18:20.610 --> 18:22.830
Coco, what did you...

18:29.630 --> 18:31.610
Thank goodness!

18:31.610 --> 18:32.280
Hang on!

18:32.280 --> 18:33.890
I'm so glad it worked!

18:33.890 --> 18:35.640
I was so scared down there!

18:36.060 --> 18:40.890
I'm really, really... really glad!

18:40.890 --> 18:43.160
Hey, knock it off!

18:43.160 --> 18:46.920
And what exactly did you do down there?

18:48.930 --> 18:50.900
What is this?

18:51.460 --> 18:52.690
Sand?

18:53.650 --> 18:54.890
Yeah!

18:54.890 --> 18:56.560
I remembered how you guys

18:56.560 --> 18:59.620
used that rock-breaking spell 
to save us before!

19:00.920 --> 19:01.910
Of course!

19:02.620 --> 19:06.720
Even with a small Seal, the Wall Breaker 
could easily pulverize the rock

19:06.720 --> 19:09.320
without hurting the person below.

19:09.960 --> 19:11.460
That's right.

19:11.460 --> 19:14.220
I couldn't help back then,

19:14.580 --> 19:17.800
but my friends' spell saved us.

19:18.160 --> 19:20.340
I couldn't have done it by myself.

19:21.710 --> 19:24.120
Seeing your shining bird reminded me.

19:25.050 --> 19:27.730
Thanks for helping me, Agott!

19:28.350 --> 19:31.910
That was a flare to call our masters back.

19:31.910 --> 19:34.490
I wasn't just doing it for you.

19:34.490 --> 19:37.490
And since when are we friends?!

19:43.010 --> 19:45.230
I really am glad...

19:46.420 --> 19:48.710
that Custas was saved.

19:50.350 --> 19:53.410
And someday, maybe... my mother, too...

19:55.160 --> 19:59.410
No. I know she will!

20:02.500 --> 20:03.700
Coco...

20:20.570 --> 20:22.760
Wh-What is this?!

20:23.380 --> 20:25.740
Silverwhite Capture Pennants...

20:26.770 --> 20:29.330
Scarlet cloaks...

20:30.160 --> 20:31.640
And winged caps...

20:33.970 --> 20:35.130
Can it be...

20:35.590 --> 20:36.890
The Knights Moralis?!

20:38.130 --> 20:39.560
Who might you be?

20:40.850 --> 20:44.000
Were you the one who cast that spell?

20:44.590 --> 20:46.310
Or was it you?

20:47.970 --> 20:51.060
Even if you are children, 
you'll get no mercy from me.

20:51.230 --> 20:55.400
Which of you is collaborating 
with the Brimmed Caps?

20:56.340 --> 20:57.400
It's not like that!

20:57.400 --> 20:59.780
We're not Brimmed Caps!

20:59.780 --> 21:02.030
We didn't use any forbidden magic, either!

21:02.030 --> 21:04.260
We used magic to help people!

21:05.400 --> 21:06.790
Are you sure?

21:07.390 --> 21:08.790
Look down there.

21:18.520 --> 21:22.350
Wh-What is all that?

21:23.810 --> 21:25.460
I didn't just change the rock...

21:25.460 --> 21:29.310
I turned the whole area, right 
down to the riverbed, into sand?

21:31.070 --> 21:34.240
And the river itself 
is vaporizing into fog...

21:36.700 --> 21:38.220
No...

21:38.220 --> 21:41.390
That's not the spell I drew.

21:41.390 --> 21:45.190
I see. So it was your spell, then?

21:46.540 --> 21:50.240
An apprentice like you couldn't 
have drawn a spell of this size

21:50.240 --> 21:53.740
without violating a taboo.

21:55.840 --> 21:58.830
The laws of the Day of the Pact 
are inviolable.

21:59.680 --> 22:02.420
Your punishment is oblivion.

23:35.480 --> 23:40.070
Episode 8:

23:35.480 --> 23:40.070
The Misgivings of the Knights Moralis
